# Store text as LF in the repository and check it out as LF everywhere, so
# Windows and POSIX clones agree and Git stops warning about CRLF round-trips.
* text=auto eol=lf

# HL7 payloads are the exception: segment terminators are semantic, and many
# real feeds terminate segments with CRLF. Under the rule above, Git rewrites
# those to bare LF on check-in -- silently altering the message. Disable all
# conversion for data files. `!eol` is required alongside `-text` because the
# eol attribute otherwise applies on its own.
*.hl7 -text !eol
*.dat -text !eol
*.ndjson -text !eol
